title type replacement: a directory becomes a file, and a file a directory

# The last emission case neither compiler has crossed.
#
# Off-of replaces a directory with a file and a file with a
# directory, at the same two names. Onto is quiet throughout, so
# nothing conflicts and nothing is held; the fixture is entirely
# about what a type change compiles to.
#
# It is a realization question before it is an emission one. A pool
# needs a SAME-TYPE onto contributor to reuse an onto dnode, and at
# both names onto holds the other type -- so neither output pool can
# take the dnode sitting at its name, however much the name matches.
#
# The directory being replaced also has a child, so the old subtree
# has to come apart before its own entry can go: the children-first
# arrow, in the smallest fixture that has one.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: dir2file/
      3-100: child = cv0
    4-100: file2dir = fv0

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: dir2file/
      3-100: child = cv0
    4-100: file2dir = fv0

tree offof
  1-1: /
    5-300: dir2file = nv0
    6-300: file2dir/
      7-300: newchild = ncv0
